# Package-scoped exception to the repo-root `build/` ignore rule (.gitignore:57).
#
# `apps/desktop/build/` contains build-time TypeScript scripts (e.g.
# `assert-webprefs.ts`) that ship with the source tree and run as part of
# `pnpm build` to enforce Spec-023 §Security Hardening Baseline invariants.
# These scripts are first-class source code, not generated artifacts, so they
# must be tracked. The repo-root rule was authored before any package needed a
# `build/` source dir; this narrow un-ignore re-admits the desktop one.
!build/

# Package-scoped build-artifact ignore for `apps/desktop/out/`.
#
# `out/` is the emit target for two generators wired in Plan-023 Phase 1:
#   • The renderer composite project's `tsc -b` pass writes to `out/renderer/`
#     (apps/desktop/src/renderer/tsconfig.json §compilerOptions.outDir).
#   • electron-vite's renderer bundle and main/preload chunks land under
#     `out/` per the electron-vite default layout.
#
# Leading slash anchors the rule to the package root (parallel to `!build/`
# above) so a stray `out/` lower in the tree wouldn't accidentally match.
# Repo-root .gitignore covers `dist/` and `node_modules/` but not `out/`, so
# this package-scoped rule keeps the artifact-vs-source ignore policy local
# to the package that produces the artifact.
/out/
